\sectd \ltrsect\linex0\endnhere\sectlinegrid360\sectdefaultcl\sectrsid15235679\sftnbj {\rtlch\fcs1 \af31507 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid5117326\charrsid5117326 
\par PART ONE\~
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ai\af31507 \ltrch\fcs0 \i\insrsid5117326\charrsid5117326 Chorus}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af31507 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid5117326\charrsid5117326 
\par Lord, our redeemer, thou whose name in all the world is highly praised,
\par show us in this thy passion, that thou, the true and only son for evermore,
\par e'en from humiliation sore dost rise with victory crowned.
\par \~
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ai\af31507 \ltrch\fcs0 \i\insrsid5117326\charrsid5117326 Recitative}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af31507 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid5117326\charrsid5117326 
\par Jesus went with his disciples over the brook Cedron, where was a garden,
\par into which he entered and his disciples.
\par Judas Iscariot, which did betray him, also knew the place: for Jesus resorted
\par thither oft together with his disciples. And when Judas had received a band
\par of men and of officers from the chief priests and the Pharisees, he cometh
\par thither with lanterns, torches and with weapons. Then as Jesus knew of all
\par things that were to come upon him, he went forth and said unto them,
\par Whom seek ye? And they answered him,
\par \~
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ai\af31507 \ltrch\fcs0 \i\insrsid5117326\charrsid5117326 Chorus}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af31507 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid5117326\charrsid5117326 
\par Jesus of Nazareth.
\par \~
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ai\af31507 \ltrch\fcs0 \i\insrsid5117326\charrsid5117326 Recitative}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af31507 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid5117326\charrsid5117326 
\par Jesus saith to them, I am he.
\par Judas also, which did betray him, was standing by them. As soon then as
\par he had said, I am he, they all moved backward, and fell to the ground.
\par Then asked he them a second time, Whom seek ye? Again they said,
\par \~
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ai\af31507 \ltrch\fcs0 \i\insrsid5117326\charrsid5117326 Chorus}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af31507 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid5117326\charrsid5117326 
\par Jesus of Nazareth.
\par \~
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ai\af31507 \ltrch\fcs0 \i\insrsid5117326\charrsid5117326 Recitative}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af31507 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid5117326\charrsid5117326 
\par Jesus answered them, I told you but now, I am he: if you are seeking me,
\par let these men go their way.
\par \~
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ai\af31507 \ltrch\fcs0 \i\insrsid5117326\charrsid5117326 Chorale}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af31507 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid5117326\charrsid5117326 
\par O wondrous love, o love of depth unbounded.
\par That brought thee here by sin and grief surrounded.
\par I live, the pleasures of this world enjoying,
\par And thou art dying.
\par \~
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ai\af31507 \ltrch\fcs0 \i\insrsid5117326\charrsid5117326 Recitative}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af31507 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid5117326\charrsid5117326 
\par So that the word might be fulfilled, which he had spoken: Of them that
\par thou gavest to me, of them have I lost not one.
\par Then Simon Peter having a sword, he drew it out and smote at the high
\par priest's serving-man, and cut his right ear off. And his name was Malchus.
\par Then said Jesus to Peter, Put up thy sword in the scabbard. Shall I not drink
\par that cup, the which my Father has given me?
\par \~
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ai\af31507 \ltrch\fcs0 \i\insrsid5117326\charrsid5117326 Chorale}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af31507 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid5117326\charrsid5117326 
\par Thy will, o Lord our God, be done
\par On earth, as round thy heavenly throne.
\par In time of sorrow patience give,
\par Obedient ever make us live.
\par With thy restraining spirit fill
\par Each heart that strives against thy will.
\par \~
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ai\af31507 \ltrch\fcs0 \i\insrsid5117326\charrsid5117326 Recitative}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af31507 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid5117326\charrsid5117326 
\par The band then, together with the captain and the servants of the Jews, took
\par hold on Jesus, and bound him fast, and led him away at first unto Annas,
\par who was Caiaphas' father-in-law, who that same year was the high priest.
\par Now it was Caiaphas, who counselled the Jews, that it was expedient that
\par one man should die for the people.
\par \~
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ai\af31507 \ltrch\fcs0 \i\insrsid5117326\charrsid5117326 Aria}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af31507 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid5117326\charrsid5117326 
\par From the bondage of transgression to give me freedom is my holy saviour
\par bound.
\par And from every taint of sickness fully to heal me doth he bear this grievous
\par wound.
\par \~
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ai\af31507 \ltrch\fcs0 \i\insrsid5117326\charrsid5117326 Recitative}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af31507 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid5117326\charrsid5117326 
\par Simon Peter also followed Jesus afar with another disciple.
\par \~
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ai\af31507 \ltrch\fcs0 \i\insrsid5117326\charrsid5117326 Aria}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af31507 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid5117326\charrsid5117326 
\par I follow thee also, my saviour, with gladness.
\par Go not from my sight, my life and my light.
\par Then show me thy way, and let me not stray,
\par Thyself, Lord, to guide me, to draw me, to help me.
\par \~
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ai\af31507 \ltrch\fcs0 \i\insrsid5117326\charrsid5117326 Recitative}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af31507 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid5117326\charrsid5117326 
\par Now that same disciple was known unto the high priest, and went with
\par Jesus within to the palace of the high priest. But Peter stood outside at the
\par door. And then the other disciple, who was known unto the high priest.
\par went out, and spake unto her that kept the door, and brought Peter also
\par within. Then said the maid that kept the door to Peter. Art thou not one
\par of this man's disciples? He saith, I am not.
\par The officers and the servants that stood there had made them a fire of
\par coals; for it was cold; and they warmed themselves: Peter also stood among
\par them and warmed himself.
\par Then the high priest questioned Jesus of his disciples, and of his doctrine.
\par Jesus made answer to him. I always spake openly and freely to the world, and at all times I have spoken in the synagogue and in the temple, whither the Jews always resort; and in secret I have spoken nothing. Wherefore askest thou me? Ask ye rather them w
ho have heard me speaking, what it is that I have spoken. Behold, they themselves know what I have spoken to them.
\par And when he had thus spoken, an officer who was standing by struck
\par Jesus with the palm of his hand, and said, Dost thou answer then the high
\par Priest so? Jesus answered unto him, If I had spoken evil, then do thou bear witness of the evil: but if I had spoken well, why smites thou me?
\par \~
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ai\af31507 \ltrch\fcs0 \i\insrsid5117326\charrsid5117326 Chorale}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af31507 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid5117326\charrsid5117326 
\par O Lord. who dares to smite thee,
\par And falsely to indict thee,
\par Deride and mock thee also.
\par We and our sons in blindness
\par Have scorned God's loving-kindness,
\par But spot of sin didst thou not know.
\par I, I have done this wounding
\par By countless sins abounding
\par As sands upon the shore.
\par 'Twas I, Lord, who forsook thee,
\par When cruel soldiers took thee,
\par To bring thee tribulation sore.
\par \~
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ai\af31507 \ltrch\fcs0 \i\insrsid5117326\charrsid5117326 Recitative}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af31507 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid5117326\charrsid5117326 
\par And Annas sent him bound unto the high priest Caiaphas. Simon Peter
\par stood and warmed himself. Then said they unto him.
\par \~
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ai\af31507 \ltrch\fcs0 \i\insrsid5117326\charrsid5117326 Chorus}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af31507 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid5117326\charrsid5117326 
\par Art thou not one of his disciples?
\par \~
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ai\af31507 \ltrch\fcs0 \i\insrsid5117326\charrsid5117326 Recitative}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af31507 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid5117326\charrsid5117326 
\par He denied it and said, I am not. And a certain high priest's servant. one that
\par was a kinsman of him whose ear Peter had cut off. saith. Did I not see thee
\par in the garden with him}{\rtlch\fcs1 \ai\af31507 \ltrch\fcs0 \i\insrsid5117326\charrsid5117326 ?\~ }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af31507 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid5117326\charrsid5117326 Then did Peter deny a third time. and while he
\par spake immediately the cock crew.
\par Then did Peter think upon the words of Jesus: and he went forth and wept
\par Bitterly.
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ai\af31507 \ltrch\fcs0 \i\insrsid5117326\charrsid5117326 Aria}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af31507 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid5117326\charrsid5117326 
\par Ah! my soul, o whither wilt thou fly? Where shall I seek for comfort?
\par Shall I stay, or depart and leave the hills and mountains far behind me?
\par In the world is no relief; on my heart remains the burden; mine the evil
\par deed, since the servant has denied his Lord.
\par \~
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ai\af31507 \ltrch\fcs0 \i\insrsid5117326\charrsid5117326 Chorale}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af31507 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid5117326\charrsid5117326 
\par Peter, faithless, thrice denies
\par That his Lord he knoweth.
\par When he meets those earnest eyes,
\par Weeping, forth he goeth.
\par Jesu, when I will not turn,
\par Look on me in kindness;
\par Make my heart within me burn,
\par Rouse me from my blindness.
\par \~
\par PART TWO
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ai\af31507 \ltrch\fcs0 \i\insrsid5117326\charrsid5117326 Chorale}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af31507 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid5117326\charrsid5117326 
\par Christ, the Lord of life and light,
\par Saviour meek and lowly,
\par Taken like a thief at night,
\par Bound by hands unholy.
\par See the saviour crowned with thorn,
\par Falsely judged and smitten;
\par See the soldiers spit and scorn,
\par As by prophet written.
\par \~
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ai\af31507 \ltrch\fcs0 \i\insrsid5117326\charrsid5117326 Recitative}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af31507 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid5117326\charrsid5117326 
\par Then led they Jesus from Caiaphas to the judgement hall; and it was early;
\par and they went not into the judgement hall lest they should become defiled;
\par but that they might keep the passover.
\par And then went Pilate out unto them and said, What accusation bring ye
\par now against this man? And they answered and said unto him,
\par \~
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ai\af31507 \ltrch\fcs0 \i\insrsid5117326\charrsid5117326 Chorus}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af31507 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid5117326\charrsid5117326 
\par If this man were not a malefactor, to thee we would not have delivered
\par him.
\par \~
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ai\af31507 \ltrch\fcs0 \i\insrsid5117326\charrsid5117326 Recitative}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af31507 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid5117326\charrsid5117326 
\par And Pilate said unto them, Then take ye him away, and judge ye him according
\par to your law. Then answered the Jews unto him,
\par \~
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ai\af31507 \ltrch\fcs0 \i\insrsid5117326\charrsid5117326 Chorus}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af31507 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid5117326\charrsid5117326 
\par It is not lawful for us to put a man to death.
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ai\af31507 \ltrch\fcs0 \i\insrsid5117326\charrsid5117326 Recitative}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af31507 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid5117326\charrsid5117326 
\par That the saying of Jesus might be fulfilled, which he had spoken, when he
\par signified by what manner of death he should die.
\par Then Pilate entered again into the judgement hall, called Jesus, and said
\par to him, Art thou the King of the Jews? Jesus answered him, Dost thou say
\par this of thyself, or did others rather tell it thee of me? And Pilate answered,
\par Am I a Jew. The chief priests and thine own nation have delivered thee
\par unto me: what hast thou done. And Jesus answered, My kingdom is not
\par of this world: if my kingdom were of this world, then my servants would
\par be fighting, that I should not be delivered unto the Jews; but now is my
\par kingdom not from hence.
\par \~
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ai\af31507 \ltrch\fcs0 \i\insrsid5117326\charrsid5117326 Chorale}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af31507 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid5117326\charrsid5117326 
\par O mighty king. eternal is thy glory,
\par How can I fitly tell thy wondrous story?
\par No heart can find a worthy gift to proffer,
\par None dare I offer.
\par In vain on thy perfections, Lord, I ponder,
\par Thy boundless mercy still transcends my wonder.
\par How then shall I do aught that can delight thee,
\par Or e'er requite thee?
\par \~
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ai\af31507 \ltrch\fcs0 \i\insrsid5117326\charrsid5117326 Recitative}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af31507 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid5117326\charrsid5117326 
\par And Pilate said unto him, Art thou indeed then a king? Jesus answered him,
\par Thou sayest, I am a king. To this end was I born, and came into the world,
\par that I should witness to the truth. Each one that is of the truth heareth my
\par voice. Pilate saith unto him, What is truth?
\par And when he had thus spoken, he went out again to the Jews, and said
\par unto them. I find in him no fault at all. But ye have a custom at this time.
\par that I should release one unto you. Will ye, now that I should release the
\par King of the Jews?
\par Then cried they all with one accord, saying,
\par \~
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ai\af31507 \ltrch\fcs0 \i\insrsid5117326\charrsid5117326 Chorus}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af31507 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid5117326\charrsid5117326 
\par Not this man, no, not this. Not this man, rather Barabbas.
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ai\af31507 \ltrch\fcs0 \i\insrsid5117326\charrsid5117326 \~}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af31507 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid5117326\charrsid5117326 
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ai\af31507 \ltrch\fcs0 \i\insrsid5117326\charrsid5117326 Recitative}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af31507 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid5117326\charrsid5117326 
\par Now Barabbas was a robber.
\par Then Pilate therefore took Jesus and scourged him.
\par \~
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ai\af31507 \ltrch\fcs0 \i\insrsid5117326\charrsid5117326 Arioso}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af31507 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid5117326\charrsid5117326 
\par Consider, o my soul, with fearful joy consider, with bitter anguish in thy
\par heart afflicted, thy highest good is Jesus' sorrow. For thee, from the thorns
\par that pierce him, lo! heaven-blessed roses spring; thou canst the sweetest
\par fruit from his sharp wormwood gather. Then look for evermore to him.
\par \~
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ai\af31507 \ltrch\fcs0 \i\insrsid5117326\charrsid5117326 Aria}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af31507 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid5117326\charrsid5117326 
\par Behold ye, how his limbs with blood are stained, a wondrous vision of
\par heaven's glory bright. So then, after the heavy torrents of our transgression
\par cease their flowing, shines out the beauteous rainbow, a sign of God's unending love.
\par \~
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ai\af31507 \ltrch\fcs0 \i\insrsid5117326\charrsid5117326 Recitative}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af31507 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid5117326\charrsid5117326 
\par And when the soldiers had plaited a crown of thorns, they put it upon his
\par head, and put on him a purple robe, and said,
\par \~
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ai\af31507 \ltrch\fcs0 \i\insrsid5117326\charrsid5117326 Chorus}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af31507 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid5117326\charrsid5117326 
\par We salute thee, mighty King of Judah.
\par \~
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ai\af31507 \ltrch\fcs0 \i\insrsid5117326\charrsid5117326 Recitative}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af31507 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid5117326\charrsid5117326 
\par And they smote him with their hands. Then Pilate therefore went forth
\par again and said unto them, Behold, I bring him hither unto you, that ye may
\par know that I find no fault in him.
\par And then did Jesus come forth, wearing the crown of thorns and the
\par purple robe. And he said to them, Behold the man! And forthwith, when
\par the priests and officers saw him, they cried out and said,
\par \~
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ai\af31507 \ltrch\fcs0 \i\insrsid5117326\charrsid5117326 Chorus}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af31507 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid5117326\charrsid5117326 
\par Crucify.
\par \~
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ai\af31507 \ltrch\fcs0 \i\insrsid5117326\charrsid5117326 Recitative}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af31507 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid5117326\charrsid5117326 
\par And Pilate saith unto them, Take ye him away, and crucify him: for I find
\par no fault at all in him. The Jews therefore answered him,
\par \~
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ai\af31507 \ltrch\fcs0 \i\insrsid5117326\charrsid5117326 Chorus}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af31507 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid5117326\charrsid5117326 
\par We have an old decree, and by that decree he must die; for he made himself
\par the Son of God most high.
\par \~
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ai\af31507 \ltrch\fcs0 \i\insrsid5117326\charrsid5117326 Recitative}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af31507 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid5117326\charrsid5117326 
\par And when Pilate heard that saying, he was the more afraid; and he went
\par in again to the judgement hall, and said to Jesus, From whence then art
\par thou?
\par But Jesus gave him no answer. Then said Pilate to him, Speakest thou not
\par unto me? Knowest thou not that I have the power to crucify, and also the
\par power to release thee? Jesus made answer, Thou couldest have no power
\par against me, had it not been given to thee from above: therefore he that
\par delivered me unto thee hath the greater sin.
\par From thenceforth Pilate therefore sought how he might release him.
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ai\af31507 \ltrch\fcs0 \i\insrsid5117326\charrsid5117326 Chorale}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af31507 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid5117326\charrsid5117326 
\par Thy bonds, o Son of God most high,
\par Have perfect freedom brought us;
\par And free, we to thy throne come nigh,
\par As thou by grace hast taught us.
\par Hadst thou disdained this bondage sore.
\par 'vV e had been bound for evermore.
\par \~
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ai\af31507 \ltrch\fcs0 \i\insrsid5117326\charrsid5117326 Recitative}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af31507 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid5117326\charrsid5117326 
\par But the Jews cried out and said,
\par \~
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ai\af31507 \ltrch\fcs0 \i\insrsid5117326\charrsid5117326 Chorus}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af31507 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid5117326\charrsid5117326 
\par If thou let this man go, then art thou no friend of Caesar; for the man that
\par maketh himself a king is enemy to Caesar.
\par \~
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ai\af31507 \ltrch\fcs0 \i\insrsid5117326\charrsid5117326 Recitative}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af31507 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid5117326\charrsid5117326 
\par And when Pilate heard that saying, he brought Jesus forth, and sat down
\par upon the judgement seat in a place that is called High Pavement, that is in
\par the Hebrew Gabbatha. And it was the preparation of the passover, about
\par the sixth hour. And he saith unto the Jews, Behold the King of the Jews!
\par They cried out,
\par \~
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ai\af31507 \ltrch\fcs0 \i\insrsid5117326\charrsid5117326 Chorus}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af31507 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid5117326\charrsid5117326 
\par Away with him, crucify him.
\par \~
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ai\af31507 \ltrch\fcs0 \i\insrsid5117326\charrsid5117326 Recitative}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af31507 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid5117326\charrsid5117326 
\par Pilate saith unto them, Shall I crucify your king? The chief priests answered
\par and said,
\par \~
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ai\af31507 \ltrch\fcs0 \i\insrsid5117326\charrsid5117326 Chorus}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af31507 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid5117326\charrsid5117326 
\par We have no king but Caesar.
\par \~
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ai\af31507 \ltrch\fcs0 \i\insrsid5117326\charrsid5117326 Recitative}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af31507 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid5117326\charrsid5117326 
\par Then delivered he him unto them, that they might crucify him. And they
\par took hold on Jesus, and led him away. And he bearing his cross went forth
\par unto a place called the place of a skull, which is called in the Hebrew
\par Golgotha.
\par \~
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ai\af31507 \ltrch\fcs0 \i\insrsid5117326\charrsid5117326 Aria with chorus}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af31507 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid5117326\charrsid5117326 
\par Haste, ye deeply wounded spirits, come and bring your heavy burdens.
\par O where?
\par To Golgotha.
\par Take, o take the wings of faith and fly.
\par O where?
\par To the cross of Jesus; find relief and healing there.
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ai\af31507 \ltrch\fcs0 \i\insrsid5117326\charrsid5117326 Recitative}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af31507 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid5117326\charrsid5117326 
\par And there crucified they him, and with him two others, on either side one
\par and Jesus in the midst. And Pilate wrote out a title and put it upon the cross.
\par And the writing was, JESUS OF AZARETH THE KING OF THE JEWS.
\par This title then read many of the Jews, for the place was nigh unto the
\par city, where Jesus was crucified. And it was written in the Hebrew and the
\par Greek, and in Latin also.
\par Then said the chief priests of the Jews unto Pilate,
\par \~
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ai\af31507 \ltrch\fcs0 \i\insrsid5117326\charrsid5117326 Chorus}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af31507 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid5117326\charrsid5117326 
\par Write thou not the King of Judah, rather write thou that he hath said, I am
\par the King of Judah.
\par \~
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ai\af31507 \ltrch\fcs0 \i\insrsid5117326\charrsid5117326 Recitative}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af31507 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid5117326\charrsid5117326 
\par But Pilate made answer, What I have written I have written.
\par \~
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ai\af31507 \ltrch\fcs0 \i\insrsid5117326\charrsid5117326 Chorale}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af31507 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid5117326\charrsid5117326 
\par Within my inmost being
\par Thy name and cross alone,
\par (The light of all my seeing),
\par Prevailing influence own .
\par O breathe this comfort o'er me
\par When low in grief I lie,
\par That thou, Lord Jesu, for me
\par Hast given thyself to die.
\par \~
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ai\af31507 \ltrch\fcs0 \i\insrsid5117326\charrsid5117326 Recitative}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af31507 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid5117326\charrsid5117326 
\par And then did the soldiers, after they had crucified Jesus, take hold of his
\par garments and made four parts, unto every soldier each a part; and also
\par his coat.
\par The coat was however without seam, and from the top was woven
\par through and through. They said therefore one to another,
\par \~
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ai\af31507 \ltrch\fcs0 \i\insrsid5117326\charrsid5117326 Chorus}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af31507 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid5117326\charrsid5117326 
\par Let us therefore not divide it, but cast lots for it, whose it shall be.
\par \~
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ai\af31507 \ltrch\fcs0 \i\insrsid5117326\charrsid5117326 Recitative}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af31507 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid5117326\charrsid5117326 
\par So that the scripture might be fulfilled, which is written: They parted all
\par my raiment among them, and over my vesture did they cast lots. These
\par things therefore the soldiers did.
\par Now standing there by the cross of Jesus was his mother, and his mother's
\par sister Mary, Cleophas' wife, also Mary Magdalene. And when Jesus there-
\par fore saw his mother, and the disciple standing by her, whom he loved, he sait unto his mother, Woman, behold thy son! And he saith to the disciple, Behold thy mother!
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ai\af31507 \ltrch\fcs0 \i\insrsid5117326\charrsid5117326 Chorale}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af31507 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid5117326\charrsid5117326 
\par While his parting spirit sinks
\par Ere its flight be taken, Jesu son his mother thinks, Lest she be forsaken.
\par Hearts that emulate his love
\par They shall rise to realms above,
\par Where he liveth ever.
\par \~
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ai\af31507 \ltrch\fcs0 \i\insrsid5117326\charrsid5117326 Recitative}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af31507 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid5117326\charrsid5117326 
\par And from that hour he took her unto his own home.
\par After this, as Jesus knew that now all was accomplished, that the scripture
\par might be fulfilled, he saith, I thirst. There was near a vessel full of vinegar:
\par they filled therefore a sponge with the vinegar, and put it upon hyssop, and
\par put it thereupon to his mouth. And when Jesus had received of the vinegar.
\par he said, It is finished.
\par \~
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ai\af31507 \ltrch\fcs0 \i\insrsid5117326\charrsid5117326 Aria}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af31507 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid5117326\charrsid5117326 
\par All is fulfilled. O rest for all afflicted spirits.
\par This night of woe makes me upon my last hour ponder.
\par Victorious Judah's hero comes, and ends the fight.
\par It is finished.
\par \~
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ai\af31507 \ltrch\fcs0 \i\insrsid5117326\charrsid5117326 Recitative}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af31507 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid5117326\charrsid5117326 
\par And he bowed his head and was gone.
\par \~
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ai\af31507 \ltrch\fcs0 \i\insrsid5117326\charrsid5117326 Aria with chorus}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af31507 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid5117326\charrsid5117326 
\par Beloved saviour, wilt thou answer
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ai\af31507 \ltrch\fcs0 \i\insrsid5117326\charrsid5117326 As }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af31507 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid5117326\charrsid5117326 thou hast now the cross endured,
\par And thyself hast said, It is finished.
\par Am I from death delivered?
\par Can I through thy eternal merit
\par The heavenly realm inherit?
\par Shall all the world redemption see?
\par Thou canst for anguish now say nothing.
\par \~
\par Yet thou dost bow thy head and say,
\par In silence, yea.
\par Jesu, thou who knewest death.
\par Livest now forever.
\par When I yield my dying breath.
\par Lord, forsake me never.
\par Other savior need I none,
\par Since thou dost receive me.
\par Lord, to share what thou hast won, Of thy mercy give me.
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af31507 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\insrsid5117326\charrsid5117326 \~}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af31507 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid5117326\charrsid5117326 
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ai\af31507 \ltrch\fcs0 \i\insrsid5117326\charrsid5117326 Recitative}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af31507 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid5117326\charrsid5117326 
\par And then behold, the veil of the temple, as rent into t, twain e\rquote en from the
\par top unto the bottom; and the earth did quake, and the rocks were rent;
\par and the graves were opened up, and there arose many bodies of the saints.
\par \~
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ai\af31507 \ltrch\fcs0 \i\insrsid5117326\charrsid5117326 Arioso}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af31507 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid5117326\charrsid5117326 
\par My heart, behold how all the world at Jesus' sufferings likewise suffers.
\par The sun his beams in sorrow covers, the veil divides, the rocks are rent.
\par The earth doth quake, the graves are opened, when they behold the creator
\par dying. And as for thee. what wilt thou do?
\par \~
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ai\af31507 \ltrch\fcs0 \i\insrsid5117326\charrsid5117326 Aria}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af31507 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid5117326\charrsid5117326 
\par Dissolve now, my spirit, in bitterest mourning, the highest to honour. Pro
\par claim to the world and to heaven thy grief: thy Jesus is dead.
\par \~
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ai\af31507 \ltrch\fcs0 \i\insrsid5117326\charrsid5117326 Recitative}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af31507 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid5117326\charrsid5117326 
\par The Jews therefore, because it was the preparation, that the bodies should
\par not remain upon the cross on the Sabbath day (for that Sabbath day was an
\par high day), besought Pilate that their legs might be broken, and that they
\par might be taken away. Then came the soldiers, and brake the legs of the first
\par one, and of the other who was crucified with him. But when they were come
\par to Jesus, and they saw that he was already dead, they brake not his legs;
\par but one of the soldiers pierced his side with a spear, and forthwith came
\par there out blood and water.
\par And he that saw it, he also bare witness and his witness is true: and
\par the same man knoweth that that which he saith is true, that ye might
\par believe. For all these things were done, so that the scripture might be fulfilled:
\par A bone of him shall not be broken. And again another scripture
\par saith: They shall look on him whom they have pierced.
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ai\af31507 \ltrch\fcs0 \i\insrsid5117326\charrsid5117326 Chorale}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af31507 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid5117326\charrsid5117326 
\par Help us, Christ, almighty Son,
\par By thy bitter anguish,
\par Faithfully our course to run,
\par Every sin to vanquish.
\par Teach us, Lord, thy grace to know;
\par Guide our weak endeavour,
\par Our redeemer's praise to shew
\par Thankfully for ever.
\par \~
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ai\af31507 \ltrch\fcs0 \i\insrsid5117326\charrsid5117326 Recitative}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af31507 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid5117326\charrsid5117326 
\par And after this Joseph of Arimath~a. being a disciple of Jesus, but secretly
\par for fear of the Jews, besought Pilate that he might take the body of Jesus :
\par and Pilate gave him leave. He therefore came, and took the body of Jesus
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af31507 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\insrsid5117326\charrsid5117326 away,}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af31507 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid5117326\charrsid5117326 
\par There came also then Niodemus, he who at first had come to Jesus in
\par the night, and brought a mixture of myrrh and of aloes, about a hundred
\par pound weight. And they took the body of Jesus, and wound it in the linen
\par clothes with the spices also, as is the manner of the Jews to bury. Now there,
\par as in the place where he was crucified a garden, and in the garden a new
\par tomb, wherein never yet a man was laid. There therefore laid they Jesus,
\par because of the Jews' preparation; for the tomb was nigh at hand.
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ai\af31507 \ltrch\fcs0 \i\insrsid5117326\charrsid5117326 \~}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af31507 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid5117326\charrsid5117326 
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ai\af31507 \ltrch\fcs0 \i\insrsid5117326\charrsid5117326 Chorus}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af31507 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid5117326\charrsid5117326 
\par Rest calm, o body pure and holy,
\par For I no longer shall bewail thee;
\par And bring thou me to rest.
\par The grave, where all must come at last,
\par Where pain and grief no more can reach,
\par Flings wide the doors of heaven
\par And bars the gates of hell.
\par \~
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ai\af31507 \ltrch\fcs0 \i\insrsid5117326\charrsid5117326 Chorale}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af31507 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid5117326\charrsid5117326 
\par Lord Jesu, thy dear angel send,
\par Whene'er my mortal life shall end,
\par And bear my soul to heaven.
\par Within its narrow chamber keep
\par My body safe in painless sleep,
\par Till thy last call be given.
\par And when from death thou wakest me,
\par In bliss untold mine eyes shall see,
\par O Son of God, thy glorious face,
\par My saviour and my fount of grace.
\par Lord Jesu Christ, o hear thou me.
\par Thee will I praise eternally.
\par 
\par After searching for these lyrics everywhere online, I found an original album with a booklet containing the words. I am providing them here so that others can find it easier.
